{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003035-how-do-you-think-the-other-gamelines-would-remove-every-vampire-in-the-city","id":1003035,"title":"How do you think the other gamelines would remove every vampire in the city?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T13:35:06-08:00","id":1003035,"title":"How do you think the other gamelines would remove every vampire in the city?","content":"Okay, see, I'm working on a fanfic where one of the premises is that the city where the story takes place has a very cosmopolitan society of shadow people, primarily changelings, mages, and werewolves.<br /> <br /> However, I couldn't figure out a way to fit Kindred in there, thematically. So, I decided said society was founded on an anti-vampire revolt, in which the Lost got fed up with the oppression they faced from the ruling Acolytes, the mages with the Ordo Dracul's recklessness with some very dangerous Nests, and the Uratha with the toxic Resonance the Damned of the time were emitting due to increasing corruption. The three found each other, joined ranks, and began a glorious revolution/horrifying progrom that eventually drove just about every survivng vampire there to less ashen pastures after Elysium was interrupted by the Prince's planned appearence being replaced by an impromptu showing of Undead Heads Onna Stick. No, not Sticks, they only managed to get one pike enchanted to stop elder and ancillae dusting plus the &quot;raw fear&quot; aura, so they made due.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's kind of a big deal, so how would you think they went about it? Really do think that leaves stuff behind that figure into modern nights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-14-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:05:05-08:00","id":1003050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003035-how-do-you-think-the-other-gamelines-would-remove-every-vampire-in-the-city#post1003035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, see, I'm working on a fanfic where one of the premises is that the city where the story takes place has a very cosmopolitan society of shadow people, primarily changelings, mages, and werewolves.<br /> <br /> However, I couldn't figure out a way to fit Kindred in there, thematically. So, I decided said society was founded on an anti-vampire revolt, in which the Lost got fed up with the oppression they faced, the mages with the Ordo Dracul's recklessness with some very dangerous Nests, and the Uratha with the toxic Resonance the Damned of the time were emitting due to increasing corruption. The three found each other, joined ranks, and began a glorious revolution/horrifying progrom that eventually drove just about every survivng vampire there to less ashen pastures after Elysium was interrupted by the Prince's planned appearence being replaced by an impromptu showing of Undead Heads Onna Stick. No, not Sticks, they only managed to get one pike enchanted to stop elder and ancillae dusting plus the &quot;raw fear&quot; aura, so they made due.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's kind of a big deal, so how would you think they went about it? Really do think that leaves stuff behind that figure into modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages, Werewolves, Changelings all possess impressive investigative abilities. Really, they'd probably mark vampires going on their nightly behavior, track them to their Havens, then set them on fire during the daytime. There really isn't much most Kindred can do to stop a Mage with a good sympathetic connection, a Fire Spirit in Twilight, or a Changeling with the right Contracts from scorching them while under the Daysleep. Ghouls and enthralled minions can only do so much.<br /> <br /> The real question would be: what steps did they take to make sure the vampire's power structure didn't generate an enormous power vacuum? Because a bunch of puppets suddenly getting their strings cut is going to generate a lot of chaos. Wheels aren't getting grease, Vices aren't getting satisfied, marching orders aren't showing up, and blackmail is coming to light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:10:22-08:00","id":1003053,"title":"","content":"Well if I know anything about vampires, it is that they are really good at going to ground. Underground, in this case. There are reasons to not go into the sewers beyond the fact that it stinks; a place without the light of the sun, and so easily shrouded in darkness. Sure, the above alliance got the more public faces, but you can't root out vampires so easily. They have survived Inquisitions, In-Fighting, Genocidal Warpaths from the Shadow Owls, and so much more; if history h\u007fas proven anything, it is that the vampires are survivors. Sure, blood might be a bit harder to come by down there, but using the beast radar and the first level of obfuscate, small intrusions upstairs are possible. The All-Night Society isn't one to back down easily, and eventually it will take back what it is owed; all it requires is time, and what is time to a vampire?<br /> <br /> <br /> I know it isn't exactly what you asked for, but that's my take on it. Hope the story works out! Oh, and if needed I could point out how each clan fits downstairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:30:04-08:00","id":1003070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003035-how-do-you-think-the-other-gamelines-would-remove-every-vampire-in-the-city?p=1003053#post1003053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if I know anything about vampires, it is that they are really good at going to ground. Underground, in this case. There are reasons to not go into the sewers beyond the fact that it stinks; a place without the light of the sun, and so easily shrouded in darkness. Sure, the above alliance got the more public faces, but you can't root out vampires so easily. They have survived Inquisitions, In-Fighting, Genocidal Warpaths from the Shadow Owls, and so much more; if history h\u007fas proven anything, it is that the vampires are survivors. Sure, blood might be a bit harder to come by down there, but using the beast radar and the first level of obfuscate, small intrusions upstairs are possible. The All-Night Society isn't one to back down easily, and eventually it will take back what it is owed; all it requires is time, and what is time to a vampire?<br /> <br /> <br /> I know it isn't exactly what you asked for, but that's my take on it. Hope the story works out! Oh, and if needed I could point out how each clan fits downstairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the more I thought of it, the more I thought it would be a great subplot for Covenants who aren't fans of the Circle or Ordo (*cough*Sanctified*cough*) probing to see if the anger had died down enough to see if they can't convince the victors that they Aren't Like Those Kindred, get a brand new domain.<br /> <br /> So, love to hear your take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T14:43:38-08:00","id":1003080,"title":"","content":"I couldn't say about changelings, but werewolves and mages could do it with relative ease. As Vent0 points out they have incredible investigative powers. A member of the Ivory Claws on a sacred hunt can detect familial and community connections to their target, for instance. Add that with their overall disliking of undead and their physical strength and they could just do it in a great hunt. Perhaps some pack found a Helion totem that wanted to scour the city clean. If the packs formed a protectorate they do have an ability that would let them locate all other supernaturals in their territory. There's dozens of ways to work it out. Mages, obviously, have a much easier way to find out where the vampires are, though aren't as inherently 'hunty' as werewolves. You could have them working in groups if you want.<br /> <br /> Daytime is your friend, though once you start killing vampires others nearby might wake up to it, so it wouldn't necessarily be a clean sweep.<br /> <br /> Still this seems more like a past tense aspect of the story. Without telling you how to do things, you might not have to go into every detail, and it's entirely likely that, like every battle, it wasn't just repeating the same method over and over and things changed and people adapted. I think you would be okay just having some veterans and some losses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:29:44-08:00","id":1003101,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel that the annihlation of the vampire population of your city is unlikely, but something more plausible might be the all night society fading into the background and waiting to be forgotten. Sure you still have sounds in the sewers at night and those who wander in the dark alone don't come back, but the majority of the survivors stay low to the ground and out of the way. Perhaps due to the hunts on vampire blood, they've abandoned the ways of the modern nights, with it's midnight kingdoms and nightclub haunters, and they've taken up their ancient mantle of the beasts that lurk beyond the fire's light. The vampires keep to the corners and kill the occasional lamb who strays from the flock but don't try to levy assaults against the new power order. Sort of like undead Men In Black, shadowy rumors without form that disappear people who look to closely beyond the city lights.<br /> <br /> An interesting idea you might want to consider is what happens after a few years of hiding, an elder rises from their sleep. I could imagine an interesting plot hook of a new elder vampire coordinating a strike to retake the night. Vampires may not be capable of the Sabbat mass embrace tactics of yore, but they can still levy considerable forces if need by. If after sometime the new order get's to complacent a sudden Vampiric uprising could shake things up somewhat.<br /> <br /> Anyway sounds like an interesting game and I hope some of this may have been useful for you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:47:49-08:00","id":1003109,"title":"","content":"Mages make a deal with the devil and draw on the Left-Handed Tamers of Blood to target entire networks of Blood Sympathy with a single spell. The Tamers' price is high.<br /> <br /> Other mages make a deal with an Angel and summon some vengeful seraph down from the Aether to turn night into day for a few minutes at Elysium.<br /> <br /> Radical Carthians make a play to sell out the Invictus and pick up the pieces when they and their allies are gone. It doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:20:37-08:00","id":1003121,"title":"","content":"Well depending on how elaborate you wanted to get, and how much the legacy of that time matters, you could have a series of deals with spirits to hunt down and kill vampires (so new vampires need to figure out how to avoid or subvert said hunter spirits), or the Mages exploiting the sympathetic connections of Blood Ties for their &quot;Clean Sweep&quot; targeting (which would mean a small, insular, separated bloodline wouldn't have been affected).<br /> <br /> Those would help define the struggles in the current nights - how to get around such counter-measures so it doesn't happen again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:21:32-08:00","id":1003123,"title":"","content":"I don't think that sweeping the entire vampire population is so easy. Certainly Mages are great to find things, and Uratha are born hunters, but to just assume such ease is to put aside the vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> But in the end, all of this isn't all that relevant to begin with.<br /> <br /> What I have to ask is what you need for your fanfic. You started saying that the vampires didn't fit thematically. The most effective way to deal with it, so, IMHO, is to not have them at the city, and that's it. Do not think about how the vampires got vanquished there, but simply states that they never got there to begin with. Maybe something on the city make it unlikely for the development of the kindred, maybe they just never arrived. Your city doesn't need to have vampires <i>in its past</i> to begin with.<br /> <br /> Making a backstory of the vampiric annihilation can have unintended and unwelcome consequences. First of all, even driving all vampires from the place, it will bring the vampires to the forefront of the narrative, at least for a while. They will be a shadow on your story, and that can be even more deleterious to your theme than their presence to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just in case you go ahead with the war, I would go for the longer road. A full blown war would be hard, costly, very demanding in too much aspects for all the involved, and leave scars and consequences. And probably be very unsuccessful in the end. Maybe a faction of the undead used it to get rid of the other, as suggested, in a plan far older than the other supernaturals thought. But again, that wouldn't solve your primary problem as stated.<br /> <br /> Since it will be background, anyway, go for a long campaign. Too much hostility, sometimes open, too much pressure on the same resources, and a vampiric population that never was so big for such a city eventually concluded it wasn't worth it for them. Instead of a few-years war, you use a centuries-long history of difficulties, and instead of genocide, you use emigration. It's done, better, cleaner, more believable and less messy for your theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:55:41-08:00","id":1003140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003035-how-do-you-think-the-other-gamelines-would-remove-every-vampire-in-the-city?p=1003123#post1003123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that sweeping the entire vampire population is so easy. Certainly Mages are great to find things, and Uratha are born hunters, but to just assume such ease is to put aside the vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> But in the end, all of this isn't all that relevant to begin with.<br /> <br /> What I have to ask is what you need for your fanfic. You started saying that the vampires didn't fit thematically. The most effective way to deal with it, so, IMHO, is to not have them at the city, and that's it. Do not think about how the vampires got vanquished there, but simply states that they never got there to begin with. Maybe something on the city make it unlikely for the development of the kindred, maybe they just never arrived. Your city doesn't need to have vampires <i>in its past</i> to begin with.<br /> <br /> Making a backstory of the vampiric annihilation can have unintended and unwelcome consequences. First of all, even driving all vampires from the place, it will bring the vampires to the forefront of the narrative, at least for a while. They will be a shadow on your story, and that can be even more deleterious to your theme than their presence to begin with.<br /> <br /> Just in case you go ahead with the war, I would go for the longer road. A full blown war would be hard, costly, very demanding in too much aspects for all the involved, and leave scars and consequences. And probably be very unsuccessful in the end. Maybe a faction of the undead used it to get rid of the other, as suggested, in a plan far older than the other supernaturals thought. But again, that wouldn't solve your primary problem as stated.<br /> <br /> Since it will be background, anyway, go for a long campaign. Too much hostility, sometimes open, too much pressure on the same resources, and a vampiric population that never was so big for such a city eventually concluded it wasn't worth it for them. Instead of a few-years war, you use a centuries-long history of difficulties, and instead of genocide, you use emigration. It's done, better, cleaner, more believable and less messy for your theme.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, that was the intention. One of the main themes I'm going for is the subjective nature of good, and that includes when justice is less &quot;fighting evil&quot; and more &quot;staring into the Abyss&quot; (literally-the city has a <i>massive </i>Scelesti problem, and the Golden Quorum from Unbidden HQs there, so many people are attracted to a creed that supports the Wicked). Since vampires are by their own admittance incredibly pragmatic and amoral, that's where the problem lies-they don't act based on pure idealism.<br /> <br /> I never wanted it to be a stable city to begin with (really, a veteran is one of the starter villains, because he's a psycho wannabe Yakuza who only got so powerful in his Court because he's good with fire), and part of the theme of it is that the alliance was built on, to an extent, unthinking hate; the only Kindred that couldn't be negotiated with if the alliance bothered was the Circle, and even then it was mostly one particular Hierophant who nobody really mourned (although taking her out <i>was </i>a good thing-woman held victim blaming as a sacrament).<br /> <br /> And as mentioned, it wasn't so much as they were all killed so much as, well, they left after a final terrorist attack convinced the Kindred they weren't safe anymore-the <i>presence </i>has been exterminated, but that has more to do with the vampires cutting their losses than actual success. They got the Primogen, but the Prince actually survived and is now the highly popular leader of the refugees. The Ordo has left their Nests behind, but they rescued their maps and experts in the confusion, so they know exactly where they are and probably more about some of them than the alliance. The Circle of the Crone was hit the worst, because they were the main targets, but since when have the <i>Witches </i>been unfamiliar with prosecution? And of course, there is the Sanctified, who see a rich territory that was just vacated by their rivals and a danger that is already showing cracks-and one that, honestly, they feel morally obligated to fashion into a crusade state, what with its crime problem in need of a good Blood Scourge or twelve (admittedly, that's something going on in the background-if I add a vampire antagonist, he's going to be a Carthian).<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think I should have mentioned that I was looking for methods and their aftereffects. I didn't say anything about the war being even mostly successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T17:46:24-08:00","id":1003164,"title":"","content":"Hence my first question was what you need. And now I have a far clearer picture of it.<br /> <br /> This seems pretty interesting, now. But I have to disagree with you at one point:<br /> <br /> Vampires <i>claim</i> to be pragmatic and amoral.<br /> <br /> Requiem is all about this stuff. As humans doomed to feed on the lives of others, their first problem is to deal with the necessity to behave as monsters to not go too far. They struggle with the question if there is still any of the human aside memory and a mask for the Beast. They go to extremes of emotion and ideal for several reasons, from beliefs of their previous lives to the urge of self-affirmation.<br /> <br /> More than any other denizen of the shadows, they organize around ideology. Mages form Cabals and Orders first because they need a guiding line for their research. Changelings look for support against the True Fae, and to adapt to their double lives. Werewolves are instinctively drawn to packs, and need tribes to help understanding and honing their skills. Vampires look for Covenants out of sheer ideology. Covenants are all about that. The Invictus believe in the feudal system of territory, loyalty, hierarchy and favor. The Lancea velieve they are the monsters of God, Damned they are so the kine can be saved in the eternal life. The Ordo Dracul isn't only keen on knowledge or power, but driven by the idea of transcending their current state, they are the vampiric version of transhumanists. The Carthian Movement are all in for the try and development of new governing ways, always believing in the political innovation. The Circle of the Crone dedicate themselves to a bloody cult that is, in the end, counterproductive if you stop to think about all the blood they let go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:07:40-08:00","id":1003210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1003035-how-do-you-think-the-other-gamelines-would-remove-every-vampire-in-the-city?p=1003164#post1003164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence my first question was what you need. And now I have a far clearer picture of it.<br /> <br /> This seems pretty interesting, now. But I have to disagree with you at one point:<br /> <br /> Vampires <i>claim</i> to be pragmatic and amoral.<br /> <br /> Requiem is all about this stuff. As humans doomed to feed on the lives of others, their first problem is to deal with the necessity to behave as monsters to not go too far. They struggle with the question if there is still any of the human aside memory and a mask for the Beast. They go to extremes of emotion and ideal for several reasons, from beliefs of their previous lives to the urge of self-affirmation.<br /> <br /> More than any other denizen of the shadows, they organize around ideology. Mages form Cabals and Orders first because they need a guiding line for their research. Changelings look for support against the True Fae, and to adapt to their double lives. Werewolves are instinctively drawn to packs, and need tribes to help understanding and honing their skills. Vampires look for Covenants out of sheer ideology. Covenants are all about that. The Invictus believe in the feudal system of territory, loyalty, hierarchy and favor. The Lancea velieve they are the monsters of God, Damned they are so the kine can be saved in the eternal life. The Ordo Dracul isn't only keen on knowledge or power, but driven by the idea of transcending their current state, they are the vampiric version of transhumanists. The Carthian Movement are all in for the try and development of new governing ways, always believing in the political innovation. The Circle of the Crone dedicate themselves to a bloody cult that is, in the end, counterproductive if you stop to think about all the blood they let go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a very good point.<br /> <br /> I'm revising my drafts a little. Give the whole &quot;return of the Damned&quot; thing a bit more of a spectre (and a good red herring).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}